Hershey Fonts - Public Domain

The Hershey fonts were developed c. 1967 by Dr. Allen Vincent Hershey 
at the Naval Weapons Laboratory, Dahlgren, Virginia. As a work of the 
United States Government, the original font data is in the public domain.

The font data files in this directory are derived from the public domain
Hershey font definitions and can be freely used, modified, and distributed
without restriction.

References:
- Hershey, A.V. (1967). "Calligraphy for Computers". 
  Naval Weapons Laboratory Technical Report 2101.
- https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hershey_fonts

The JHF format files were sourced from:
- The MIT-licensed p5-hershey-js project (https://github.com/LingDong-/p5-hershey-js)
- The GPL-licensed hershey-fonts project (https://github.com/kamalmostafa/hershey-fonts)

Both sources treat the underlying font data as public domain.

Included Font Variants:
- Roman: Simplex (simplex.jhf), Duplex (rowmand.jhf), Triplex (rowmant.jhf)
- Gothic: German Bold (gothgbt.jhf), German (gothgrt.jhf), Italian (gothitt.jhf)
- Script: Simplex (scripts.jhf), Complex (scriptc.jhf)
- Times Italic: Regular (timesi.jhf), Bold (timesib.jhf)
